Synthetic colpkg fixtures
========================

collection.colpkg, collection_nomedia_new.colpkg, and palace.colpkg are
generated by tools/arm64-smoke/make_synthetic.py. The text, the 8 by 8 PNG,
and the 32-sample WAV are written by that program. Nothing in these three
files is copied from another deck or another repository.

The generator links unmodified rslib 26.09.3 and calls it only through
Backend::run_service_method. Each package is the current colpkg shape rslib
writes: meta version 3, a zstd-compressed schema-18 collection.anki21b, a
schema-11 collection.anki2 stub (one note, fixed guid `hattoDummy`), and a
zstd media map. Import uses collection.anki21b. The stub is what rslib always
writes beside it; the previous third-party files were the same shape, and
none of them was imported as a legacy-only package.

What each file is for:

- collection.colpkg has no media. It has nested decks, a cloze note, a
  two-card note type, a filtered deck (cards with odid set), a suspended
  card, and revlog rows whose cards still exist. Apkg export keeps those
  revlog rows.
- collection_nomedia_new.colpkg has no media and no filtered deck. It has 6
  notes and 8 cards. 88 revlog rows are stored, and 87 of them point at a
  card id that does not exist. Apkg export drops those orphans, so the
  reimported collection has 1 revlog row. That is the loss judge.py records
  for this filename.
- palace.colpkg references hatto-dot.png and hatto-tone.wav from note fields.
  It also has nested decks, a filtered deck, a suspended card, and revlog
  rows for cards that still exist. It is not an FSRS case: the host fit
  returns no parameters.

The clock for a regeneration is 2026-01-15 12:00:00 Asia/Seoul. Counts in
tools/arm64-smoke/expected.json were measured on the host by the same import
and export calls the device smoke makes. They were not recaptured on the
phone.

Files in this directory that the generator does not write
---------------------------------------------------------

